python backtest.py --timeframe 15m --bars 1000




You now have the tooling. You don't yet have an edge.
EMA crossover + RSI filter + bracket risk is one of the most studied setups on BTC, and on liquid timeframes it's very close to break-even before fees and a loser after. Walk-forward just confirmed that. The tooling is correct; the strategy is the bottleneck now.

Realistic directions that would actually matter:

Change the strategy, not the parameters. Parameter tuning can't rescue a flat expectancy. Candidates worth trying (easy to slot into strategy.py):
RSI mean-reversion: buy on RSI<30 + cross back above, sell on RSI>70 + cross back below. Works better than crossovers in ranging markets.
Breakout: donchian channel / 20-day high/low. Works better in trending markets.
MACD histogram momentum: enter on histogram sign flip only when above/below zero (trend-with-momentum).
Volatility filter: ATR-normalize SL/TP (e.g. SL = 1.5×ATR) instead of fixed %. Kills the "SL never fires in low vol, always fires in high vol" problem.
Non-BTC instruments: momentum strategies work much better on ETH/SOL/smaller caps that trend harder. Literally python walkforward.py --symbol ETH/USDT will tell you.
Strategy registry: refactor strategy.py into pluggable strategies so you can A/B them. Worth doing before you pile on more ideas.